## Claim
Text: "The Democrats want to shut down U.S. churches permanently."
Claim author: Donald Trump
Claim date: October 07, 2020
Claim origin: https://web.archive.org/web/20210714065608/https://archive.vn/HfNGi

## Initial Q&A
### 1. Is there any official policy, platform plank, or stated goal from the Democratic National Committee (DNC) or a majority of Democratic leadership that advocates for the permanent closure of churches in the United States?
Answer: Based on the search result from Politifact, there is no evidence to support this claim. The source states, "We could find no evidence that Democrats are calling for churches to be permanently closed." It further notes that during the pandemic, many states, including those governed by Republicans, implemented public health restrictions, and churches were sometimes exempted rather than singled out.

Source URL: https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2020/oct/08/donald-trump/trump-falsely-claims-democrats-want-shut-your-chur/

### 2. Have any prominent Democratic elected federal officials (e.g., President, Speaker of the House, Senate Majority Leader) publicly stated that churches should be permanently shut down?
Answer: No prominent Democratic elected federal officials have publicly stated that churches should be permanently shut down. According to a PolitiFact fact-check, "Those claims do not align with statements from Biden or other leading Democrats," and investigators "couldn't find examples of Biden or any other leading Democrats saying they wanted to prosecute churchgoers for disobeying social distancing guidelines." While some Democratic and Republican governors imposed temporary restrictions on large gatherings, including at churches, as part of COVID-19 public health measures, these were temporary measures to slow the spread of the virus—not calls to permanently close churches. Biden and other leading Democrats, including House Speaker Nancy Pelosi and Atlanta Mayor Keisha Lance Bottoms, instead focused on condemning violence and supporting peaceful protest, without targeting religious institutions.

Source URL: https://www.statesman.com/story/news/politics/elections/2020/06/24/fact-check-does-joe-biden-want-to-prosecute-churchgoers/113957728/

